  "conclusion": "Four independent current-code scratch campaigns produced no authenticated terminal. The continuous fitted-Q forest has measurable held-out signal but is not robustly superior: it won 8/10 comparable semantic-state orderings and 11/16 held-out action-realization orderings, while the structured shortest-valid-action control won 10/10 and 15/16 and had lower weighted mean absolute error on both axes. One seed produced a large continuous-value error and uncertainty spike. This completes the P3 measurement task and rejects the current treatment as route-learning acceptance.",
